{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crime and Punishment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Locked Away", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe rules and obligations through a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Past Perfect Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the Past Perfect tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />   <span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had </span>already <span class=\"strong\">gone</span> home.<br /> </span> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? Vanessa went home.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I arrived at the party.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment. </span><br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">Until recently, detectives <span class=\"strong\">had used </span>a limited number of tools to help them solve crimes. <br /></span> Detectives used a limited number of tools from the past until recently. <br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Until the 1600s, most serious criminals had been executed by hanging or exiled from their homes to faraway islands. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Petty offenders and poor people who had debts they could not repay had been sentenced to workhouses.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past Passive and Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use an active structure when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject.<br /> You use a passive structure when you want the 'receive'' of the action to be the subject. <br /><br />  You use modal verbs (<span class=\"italic\">can, could, may, might, have to</span>) to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018to') of the main verb. <br /> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">The prison staff (subject) locked prisoners (object) in their cells at night.</span><br />  Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Prisoners (subject) <span class=\"strong\">were locked</span> in their cells at night (by the prison staff).</span> <br/><br /> It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br /><br />  You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the verb to be followed by the past participle.<br /><br />   The Simple Past passive form is:<br /><br />  was/were + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The building <span class=\"strong\">was built </span>in 1993.</span><br /><br />  You can add a modal verb before the verb to be.<br /><br />  Subject + modal + To be + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The cost of their imprisonment <span class=\"strong\">could be repaid.</span></span><br /><br />  Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">could</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The system was changed in 1870.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Prisoners had to be locked in their cells at night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The cost of their imprisonment could be repaid.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "humane", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having or showing compassion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first laws demanding clean, reasonably humane prisons were passed in 1789. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about prisons.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "primitive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not developed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These prisons were very primitive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hanging ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "capital punishment; tying a rope around someone's neck and then dropping them", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most serious criminals had been executed by hanging.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": " to be exiled ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be permanently sent out of your country as punishment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most serious criminals had been exiled from their homes to faraway islands. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "workhouse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a prison in which offenders are expected to work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Petty offenders and poor people who had debts they could not repay had been sentenced to workhouses. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hard labor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "heavy manual work as punishment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In these \"open\" prisons, they had to perform hard labor, usually for the rest of their lives.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prison ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building in which people are legally held as a punishment for crimes they have committed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When people are convicted of a crime, they are often sent to prison. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sane ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not mentally ill", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All of the prisoners were supposed to be mixed together \u2013 men, women, children, the sane, and the insane.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "model ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a system or thing used as an example to follow or imitate ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There were two different models for the American prison system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cell ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small room in which a prisoner is locked up", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Prisoners worked together in total silence during the day but had to be locked in their own cells at night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "solitary confinement ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a form of imprisonment in which a prisoner is isolated from other people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Prisoners were supposed to be kept in solitary confinement day and night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10aud11", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm a list of minor crimes. Write down your ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "On your own, choose one crime and think of an appropriate but humane punishment for someone who commits this crime.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In a group, present your ideas for a punishment and be prepared to defend your choice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to your group's ideas and ask them to defend their ideas.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules, regulations, crime and punishment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what is supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things I had done or things that had happened. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my opinion about punishment.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about rules, regulations, crime and punishment. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what is supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I had done or things that had happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think prison is an effective method or punishment? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you could create a new method or punishment for criminals, what would it be? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you h