xt"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn8le03ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Decide on the appropriate punishment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le03ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn8le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn8le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "Locked Away<br /><br />When people are convicted of a crime, they are often sent to prison. That has not always been the case. Until the 1600s, most serious criminals had been executed by hanging or exiled from their homes to faraway islands. Petty offenders and poor people who had debts they could not repay had been sentenced to workhouses. In these \"open\" prisons, they had to perform hard labor, usually for the rest of their lives.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn8le03ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "In the 17th century, some European countries began imprisoning debtors and other kinds of criminals. These prisons were very primitive and all of the prisoners were supposed to be mixed together \u2013 men, women, children, the sane, and the insane \u2013 all in a single large building.", "time": "28000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn8le03ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "In the US, the first laws demanding clean, reasonably humane prisons were passed in 1789. There were two different models for the American prison system. The first was the Auburn State Prison in New York, where prisoners worked together in total silence during the day but had to be locked in their own cells at night.", "time": "48000", "id": 3}, {"image": "engenn8le03ob10re2img03.jpg", "text": "The second was the Cherry Hill Prison in Pennsylvania, where prisoners were supposed to be kept in solitary confinement day and night.\nEventually, most states adopted the Auburn State model, so the cost of their imprisonment could be repaid. This system was changed again in 1870 in order to improve prison life and make it more humane.", "time": "70000", "id": 4}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}